{"id": "EUVD-2026-45523", "enisaUuid": "58b64036-7e5f-3e51-b7a5-a1631c6fd28e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: lenovo-wmi-helpers: Fix memory leak in lwmi_dev_evaluate_int()\n\nlwmi_dev_evaluate_int() leaks output.pointer when retval == NULL (found\nby sashiko.dev [1]).\n\nFix it by moving `ret_obj = output.pointer' outside of the `if (retval)'\nblock so that it is always freed by the __free cleanup callback.\n\nNo functional change intended.", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T14:04:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-07T15:45:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce493f9261cd3f4bffe2f72481d8c3ee01c559a3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40a984dd0602e238ad893b167751620e751d1199", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c3887a134f191723b53e2a47e501b534c8723ee"], "aliases": ["GHSA-84pw-g3hf-x32j", "CVE-2026-63839"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "55974279-5485-379b-8d88-67e1953f045d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e521d16e76cd9ea99c585e064f4e7daf657b1451 <40a984dd0602e238ad893b167751620e751d1199"}, {"id": "565afd7b-d0cd-3b71-8c3a-a241d9a290ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e521d16e76cd9ea99c585e064f4e7daf657b1451 <0c3887a134f191723b53e2a47e501b534c8723ee"}, {"id": "6d4779f6-8094-3159-b5a6-34449066018e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "95cc3829-0006-3ea3-a942-b58dd137f36b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "9ab40a95-e712-3cc9-9bdf-bef6740b1d0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e521d16e76cd9ea99c585e064f4e7daf657b1451 <ce493f9261cd3f4bffe2f72481d8c3ee01c559a3"}, {"id": "a666e738-72f6-3536-9965-23f4d942e5e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "